From 279ac89f1cdab681655ad8559f1cc2ad74e71836 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:30:25 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(fixtures): a flipped setup's fixtures are judged
 against the carried stock's shape, not its box

The carried-workholding clause judged each fixture by its world AABB, so
a vise gripping a carried part's sides, or soft jaws whose nest pocket
holds it, "stood inside" the part and refused the post. The box stays the
broad phase; a fixture it flags is now read by its closed world mesh,
column by column: the Z spans the mesh puts on the column's vertical line
(new FixtureMesh::steel_on_line) against the carried material, with a
0.01 mm contact tolerance (centre line and four lines 0.01 mm beside it).
The mesh only acquits: open/refused/coarse meshes, unreadable lines, a
spent visit budget and sub-cell footprints keep the box depth. Columns
that cannot deepen the worst depth are skipped, so the scan stays bounded.

Fixes #1530

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
